This is an **Array + Block Processing** problem.

### Understand the Question

Input:

```text
1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8
K = 3
```

Divide into blocks of size 3:

```text
[1 2 3] [4 5 6] [7 8]
```

Now rotate **each block** to the right by 1.

### Block 1

```text
[1 2 3]
```

Right rotate by 1:

```text
[3 1 2]
```

### Block 2

```text
[4 5 6]
```

Right rotate by 1:

```text
[6 4 5]
```

### Block 3 (last block)

```text
[7 8]
```

Even though its size is less than K, rotate it too:

```text
[8 7]
```

Final:

```text
3 1 2 6 4 5 8 7
```

---

## Concept

For every block:

```java
start = block beginning
end   = min(start + K - 1, n - 1)
```

Store the last element.

Shift all elements one step right.

Put the stored last element at the beginning.

---

## Simple Java Solution

```java
import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        int n = sc.nextInt();
        int[] arr = new int[n];

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            arr[i] = sc.nextInt();
        }

        int k = sc.nextInt();

        /*
         Concept: Block Processing

         1. Divide array into blocks of size K.
         2. For each block:
            - Save last element
            - Shift remaining elements right by one
            - Put saved element at block start
         3. Process last incomplete block as well.
        */

        for(int start = 0; start < n; start += k) {

            int end = Math.min(start + k - 1, n - 1);

            // Block of size 1 remains unchanged
            if(start == end)
                continue;

            int last = arr[end];

            for(int i = end; i > start; i--) {
                arr[i] = arr[i - 1];
            }

            arr[start] = last;
        }

        for(int x : arr) {
            System.out.print(x + " ");
        }
    }
}
```

### Time Complexity

```text
O(n)
```

Each element is shifted at most once within its block.

